        "claim": "The DFS cycle detection can miss a cycle if a node on the cycle is already marked done (color 2) before the back edge that closes the cycle is examined, because edges to done nodes are ignored; this can happen in directed graphs where a cycle node is reached and fully explored through a path that does not include the edge that would close the cycle, causing build_order to return a topological order instead of raising CycleError.",
        "severity": "high",
